  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen editing a board, if you have your browser open on an ultrawide monitor and fullscreened, changing the layout settings such as adding a new layouts or changing the number of columns does not save. Weirdly, changing the name or breakpoint of existing layouts does save. Other settings seem to save fine, only layout is affected.\n\nReducing the browser window size allows all the setting to save properly.\n\nRunning in Docker with the standard compose file, version 1.31.0\nFirefox v 141.0.2\nUltrawide monitor 3840x1600 resolution\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. open the board settings page on an ultrawide monitor. \n2. Make sure the browser is fullscreened\n3. click on the layout section and click \"add layout\"\n4. set up the layout name, breakpoint, and columns\n5. click save\n6. navigate away from the page\n7. return to the page - the settings will have reverted\n\n### Impact\n\nNiche issue, and able to be worked around by simply making the browser window smaller, however it could be confusing.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.31.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
